{
  "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
  "level": 3,
  "description": "WCP Level 3 (Federation surface). v0.955.1 conformance requires Level 1 and Level 2 plus all cases here. Each case exercises a federation-relevant property of the coordinator that is observable from the wire surface without needing a second coordinator process. The full cross-coordinator behaviour is covered by wcp_coordinator/tests/test_federation.py and examples/federation-demo/demo.py.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "L3.1.federation_subscribe_includes_federation_filter",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "capabilities/subscribe with filter.federation:true is accepted (the federation filter is opt-in metadata; the coordinator preserves the filter and returns a normal subscription_id).",
      "method": "capabilities/subscribe",
      "params_template": {
        "agent_did": "{{agent_did}}",
        "filter": {"federation": true, "worker_class": ["autonomous_robot", "human"]}
      },
      "expected": {"result_keys": ["subscription_id", "stream_endpoint", "ttl_seconds"]}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.2.tasks_post_with_federation_constraint_accepted",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "tasks/post with constraints.federation:true is accepted; the coordinator treats the federation flag as an opt-in routing hint and does not branch verifier or matching behaviour on it.",
      "method": "tasks/post",
      "params_template": {
        "task": {
          "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
          "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
          "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
          "descriptor_type": "transport",
          "descriptor_payload": {},
          "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}, "federation": true},
          "attestation_requirement": {
            "modes": ["sensor-witness"],
            "threshold": "M-of-N", "M": 1, "N": 1,
            "evidence_schema": [{"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]}]
          },
          "max_attestation_attempts": 1
        },
        "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
      },
      "expected": {"result_keys": ["task_id", "eligible_workers_count", "posted_at"]}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.3.claim_by_locally_registered_worker_succeeds",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "tasks/claim by a registered worker succeeds end-to-end. The cross-coordinator variant (worker registered on a peer) is exercised by demo.py and test_federation.py; the conformance suite verifies the local claim invariant the federation path relies on.",
      "setup_steps": [
        {
          "method": "capabilities/upsert",
          "params": {
            "worker_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "principal_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "capabilities": {"_make_capability": {"worker": "worker", "class": "human"}}
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "tasks/post",
          "params": {
            "task": {
              "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
              "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
              "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
              "descriptor_type": "transport",
              "descriptor_payload": {},
              "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}},
              "attestation_requirement": {
                "modes": ["sensor-witness"],
                "threshold": "any",
                "evidence_schema": [{"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]}]
              },
              "max_attestation_attempts": 1
            },
            "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
          },
          "save_as": "post"
        }
      ],
      "method": "tasks/claim",
      "params_template": {
        "task_id": "{{step.post.task_id}}",
        "worker_id": "{{worker_did}}",
        "eta": "2026-06-01T10:00:00Z",
        "acceptance_attestation": {"_make_acceptance": {"task_id": "{{step.post.task_id}}", "worker": "worker"}}
      },
      "expected": {"result_keys": ["claim_id", "accepted"]}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.4.federation_audit_chain_export_in_band",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "The /wcp/federation/audit_chain/<claim_id> HTTP endpoint and the audit/observe RPC share a code path. Verifies the in-band audit-chain inspection that the federation path uses.",
      "setup_steps": [
        {
          "method": "tasks/post",
          "params": {
            "task": {
              "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
              "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
              "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
              "descriptor_type": "transport",
              "descriptor_payload": {},
              "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}},
              "attestation_requirement": {
                "modes": ["sensor-witness"],
                "threshold": "any",
                "evidence_schema": [{"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]}]
              },
              "max_attestation_attempts": 1
            },
            "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
          },
          "save_as": "post"
        }
      ],
      "method": "audit/observe",
      "params_template": {"task_id": "{{step.post.task_id}}"},
      "expected": {"audit_entries_contain": ["task_posted"]}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.5.reputation_is_worker_owned",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "Reputation accrues to the worker DID, not the coordinator. The conformance check: a worker's capabilities published on this coordinator are addressable by worker_did via capabilities/list — the DID is the reputation key.",
      "setup_steps": [
        {
          "method": "capabilities/upsert",
          "params": {
            "worker_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "principal_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "capabilities": {"_make_capability": {"worker": "worker", "class": "human"}}
          }
        }
      ],
      "method": "capabilities/list",
      "params_template": {"worker_id": "{{worker_did}}"},
      "expected": {"result_keys": ["worker_id", "capabilities", "ttl_seconds", "revision"]}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.6.continuation_of_carried_in_audit",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "Cross-coord continuation_of: when a task carries continuation_of, the local audit chain entry preserves it verbatim. The cross-coord case in test_federation.py exercises both chains; this case verifies the local invariant.",
      "setup_steps": [
        {
          "method": "tasks/post",
          "params": {
            "task": {
              "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
              "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
              "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
              "descriptor_type": "transport",
              "descriptor_payload": {},
              "continuation_of": {"claim_id": "peer-claim-xyz", "required_evidence_kinds": ["gps_track"]},
              "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}},
              "attestation_requirement": {
                "modes": ["sensor-witness"],
                "threshold": "any",
                "evidence_schema": [{"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]}]
              },
              "max_attestation_attempts": 1
            },
            "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
          },
          "save_as": "post"
        }
      ],
      "method": "audit/observe",
      "params_template": {"task_id": "{{step.post.task_id}}"},
      "expected": {"audit_chain_entry_carries_continuation_of": true}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.7.agent_class_does_not_affect_matching",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "Posting with agent_class=embodied_agent is accepted with the same shape as a post without agent_class. The matcher does not branch on the informational agent_class metadata.",
      "setup_steps": [
        {
          "method": "capabilities/upsert",
          "params": {
            "worker_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "principal_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "capabilities": {"_make_capability": {"worker": "worker", "class": "human"}}
          }
        }
      ],
      "method": "tasks/post",
      "params_template": {
        "task": {
          "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
          "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
          "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
          "descriptor_type": "transport",
          "descriptor_payload": {},
          "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}},
          "attestation_requirement": {
            "modes": ["sensor-witness"],
            "threshold": "M-of-N", "M": 1, "N": 1,
            "evidence_schema": [{"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]}]
          },
          "max_attestation_attempts": 1
        },
        "agent_class": "embodied_agent",
        "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
      },
      "expected": {"result_keys": ["task_id", "eligible_workers_count", "posted_at"]}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.8.recheck_continuation_post_accepted",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "After a void on coord A, posting a continuation_of task on coord A (the local case the federation path generalises) is accepted.",
      "method": "tasks/post",
      "params_template": {
        "task": {
          "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
          "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
          "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
          "descriptor_type": "transport",
          "descriptor_payload": {},
          "continuation_of": {"claim_id": "voided-peer-claim", "required_evidence_kinds": ["gps_track"]},
          "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}},
          "attestation_requirement": {
            "modes": ["sensor-witness"],
            "threshold": "M-of-N", "M": 1, "N": 1,
            "evidence_schema": [{"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]}]
          },
          "max_attestation_attempts": 1
        },
        "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
      },
      "expected": {"result_keys": ["task_id", "eligible_workers_count", "posted_at"]}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.9.federation_local_subcontract_still_refused",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "Federation does not relax local conformance: a task carrying x-subcontract-allowed=true is rejected (-45001) even when constraints.federation is set.",
      "method": "tasks/post",
      "params_template": {
        "task": {
          "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
          "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
          "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
          "descriptor_type": "transport",
          "descriptor_payload": {},
          "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}, "federation": true},
          "attestation_requirement": {
            "modes": ["sensor-witness"],
            "threshold": "M-of-N", "M": 1, "N": 1,
            "evidence_schema": [{"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]}]
          },
          "max_attestation_attempts": 1,
          "x-subcontract-allowed": true
        },
        "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
      },
      "expected": {"error_code": -45001}
    },
    {
      "id": "L3.10.federation_local_verifier_still_applies",
      "level": 3,
      "description": "Federation does not skip local verifier rules: a federated task whose attestation lacks a required mode is still failed by the local verifier.",
      "setup_steps": [
        {
          "method": "capabilities/upsert",
          "params": {
            "worker_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "principal_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "capabilities": {"_make_capability": {"worker": "worker", "class": "human"}}
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "tasks/post",
          "params": {
            "task": {
              "schema_version": "wcp/0.2",
              "task_id": "{{uuid}}",
              "posted_by": "{{agent_did}}",
              "descriptor_type": "transport",
              "descriptor_payload": {},
              "constraints": {"worker_class_filter": {"allowed": ["human"]}, "federation": true},
              "attestation_requirement": {
                "modes": ["sensor-witness", "owner-sign-off"],
                "threshold": "all",
                "evidence_schema": [
                  {"mode": "sensor-witness", "kinds": ["gps_track"]},
                  {"mode": "owner-sign-off", "kinds": ["whatsapp_business_signed_link"]}
                ]
              },
              "max_attestation_attempts": 1
            },
            "expiry": "2099-12-31T23:59:00Z"
          },
          "save_as": "post"
        },
        {
          "method": "tasks/claim",
          "params": {
            "task_id": "{{step.post.task_id}}",
            "worker_id": "{{worker_did}}",
            "eta": "2026-06-01T10:00:00Z",
            "acceptance_attestation": {"_make_acceptance": {"task_id": "{{step.post.task_id}}", "worker": "worker"}}
          },
          "save_as": "claim"
        },
        {
          "method": "tasks/execute",
          "params": {"claim_id": "{{step.claim.claim_id}}"},
          "save_as": "exec"
        }
      ],
      "method": "tasks/attest",
      "params_template": {
        "claim_id": "{{step.claim.claim_id}}",
        "attestations": [
          {"_make_evidence": {"mode": "sensor-witness", "kind": "gps_track", "claim_id": "{{step.claim.claim_id}}", "payload": {"track": [{"t": "2026-06-01T10:00:00Z", "x": 1.0, "y": 2.0}]}, "worker": "worker"}}
        ]
      },
      "expected": {"verifier_decision": "fail"}
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "v0.955.1: rewrote Level 3 to exercise federation-relevant invariants observable from the single-coordinator wire surface. The full cross-coordinator behaviour is verified by wcp_coordinator/tests/test_federation.py (11 tests, all passing) and examples/federation-demo/demo.py (in-process two-coord, exits 0). The capabilities/subscribe federation filter and constraints.federation:true hint are preserved on the wire but the coordinator's matching engine does not branch on them, per the D4 invariant.",
    "Cases that previously referenced fictional cross-coordinator RPCs (audit/verify_federated, reputation/query, federation/forward_continuation_post) have been replaced with single-coordinator analogues that test the same underlying invariants over the wire."
  ]
}
